<|im_start|>user
Here is a piece of text: William Przystup found a new school but will stay in the same conference.
The Michigan State freshman punter announced via Twitter Monday morning he is transferring to Nebraska. Michigan State coach Mark Dantonio said on Jan. 10 Przystup was transferring to another program as the Spartans head into the 2019 season with a logjam at the position.
Przystup, from Oviedo High School in Florida, signed with Michigan State’s 2018 recruiting class as a preferred walk-on. He was thrust into action as a true freshman last year as Michigan State battled injuries and used five different punters.
Jake Hartbarger was entering his fourth year as the starting punter but suffered a season-ending right leg injury in a Sept. 8 loss at Arizona State, resulting in backup quarterback Rocky Lombardi punting once in an emergency role. Redshirt freshman walk-on Bryce Baringer was added to the roster the following week and split time with redshirt freshman walk-on Tyler Hunt, who suffered a torn ACL in October.
Przystup made his college debut in a Nov. 10 loss to Ohio State with a 52-yard punt. He played the final four games and averaged 40.6 yards on 27 attempts with five of at least 50 yards and nine downed inside the 20-yard line.
Hartbarger is applying for a sixth year of eligibility and expected to return as the starter while Hunt and Baringer are also eligible to come back. Michigan State also added a second scholarship punter in Jack Bouwmeester, an Australian who signed with the 2019 recruiting class and is an early enrollee.
Because he appeared in only four games, Przystup can take advantage of a new NCAA rule implemented last year and use the 2018 season as a redshirt year. He will still have four years of eligibility remaining but will have to sit out the 2019 season unless he appeals and is granted immediate eligibility.
Przystup is one of two Spartans who announced after the 2018 season they are transferring. Defensive tackle Mufi Hill-Hunt in January said he is seeking a gradate transfer.

Based on the text material above, generate the response to the following quesion or instruction: Who were the other punters on Michigan State's roster last year, and what happened to each of them?<|im_end|>
